cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite
  the cross-impact balance methodology paper (Weimer-Jehle 2006) listed under
  references.
type: software
title: CrossImpactBalances.jl
version: 0.2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Morrow
    given-names: Iain
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/IainDM/CrossImpactBalances
abstract: >-
  Fast, exact cross-impact balance (CIB) scenario analysis in Julia: exhaustive
  consistency search and complete basin-of-attraction analysis on scenario
  spaces of up to hundreds of millions of combinations, with Python bindings, a
  C ABI, and a desktop application.
keywords:
  - cross-impact balance
  - scenario analysis
  - foresight
  - Julia
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Weimer-Jehle
        given-names: Wolfgang
    title: "Cross-impact balances: A system-theoretical approach to cross-impact analysis"
    journal: Technological Forecasting and Social Change
    year: 2006
    volume: 73
    issue: 4
    start: 334
    end: 361
    doi: 10.1016/j.techfore.2005.06.005
